20. Presentation Script
You can use the following script during your project demonstration:
ComicCraft Project Demonstration Script
Good morning everyone.
Today, we are demonstrating our project, ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator using Gemini Models.
ComicCraft is an AI-powered application that helps users create comics from simple story ideas. Instead of manually writing the story, developing characters, planning scenes, and creating panels separately, the user can provide a basic idea and let the system assist with the entire process.
First, we log in to the application and open the dashboard.
Here, users can create a new comic or continue working on an existing project.
Now, we will create a new comic called The Lost Robot. We select the science-fiction genre and an adventure tone. The story idea is that a college student discovers an abandoned robot beneath an old laboratory.
When we click Generate Story, the application sends the request to our backend, which communicates with the Gemini model. Gemini expands the basic idea into a structured story.
Next, we generate the characters. The system creates character profiles containing information such as their names, roles, personalities, and appearances.
The story is then divided into scenes. Each scene is further divided into individual comic panels.
For every panel, ComicCraft can generate the scene description, character actions, dialogue, narration, and visual prompt. Where the visual-generation pipeline is enabled, these prompts can also be used to create the panel artwork.
Now we open the comic editor. Here, the user has complete control over the generated content. We can edit dialogue, change narration, add or remove panels, reorder panels, and regenerate individual sections.
For example, instead of regenerating the complete comic, we can modify only Panel 2. This is possible because ComicCraft stores the comic as structured data consisting of stories, characters, scenes, and panels.
Finally, we preview the completed comic and export it.
The main technology behind the intelligent content-generation workflow is the Gemini model. The frontend provides the user interface, while the backend manages the AI service, database, authentication, and project logic.
Therefore, the complete ComicCraft workflow is:
Idea → Story → Characters → Scenes → Panels → Dialogue → Artwork → Editing → Final Comic.
This demonstrates how generative AI can assist users in transforming a simple creative idea into an editable comic.
Thank you.
This sequence gives you a complete end-to-end demonstration while also showing the technical contribution of the project rather than only displaying the final comic.

